xnu: 0092 sweet drill the silent reset funnel after the trust caches

Drill after boot#21 (0091 kernel): the console ran to
"SWEET: trust caches unavailable (Image4/AMFI not installed)" and then
the phone silently rebooted with no further fbcon output.  Patches
0010/0089 already force every panic() through the framebuffer
(sweet_early_panic / sweet_early_panic_flush print the panic story
before any panic machinery stalls), and none of their lines ever
appeared: boot#21 did not die inside a panic().  The reset happened
outside the kernel panic path: either the xnu reboot funnels
(PEHaltRestart / halt_all_cpus) were driven from a non-panic path, a
fatal CPU exception reached the EL1 vectors without panicking, or a
platform/firmware actor reset the SoC on its own (QCOM watchdog/TZ)
- or a real panic flashed past and was wiped before the phone could be
filmed.

This patch names every door with one P0092 line, everything inside
#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET) (the panic-freeze helper lives in
the pre-existing SWEET-gated sweet_early.c), so the next photo either
shows the funnel that rebooted the phone or stops at the last beat
reached:

- startup.c kernel_bootstrap_thread: explicit prints around the last
  free-standing setup calls between the trust caches and bsd_init:
  OSKextRemoveKextBootstrap, machine_lockdown, kernel_do_post,
  PE_lockdown_iokit, bsd_init enter/return.  (The pre-existing
  kernel_bootstrap_log() strings only print with STARTUP_DEBUG_VERBOSE,
  so they are silent on the real phone.)
- bsd_init.c: entry/milestones (mac_policy_initbsd, vfsinit,
  bsd_autoconf, setconf/IOFindBSDRoot, vfs_mountroot result, root
  vnode set, bsd_utaskbootstrap, done).
- iokit/bsddev/IOKitBSDInit.cpp: IOKitBSDInit entry, IOFindBSDRoot
  entry + parsed rd= value, the SWEET ufsroot0 branch.
- bsd/dev/sweet_ufs.c: sweet_ufs_rootdev entry and sweet_ufs_init
  steps (DT node, reg map, DMA block, host takeover, partition probe),
  so "SWEET UFS:" is no longer the very first signal from that file.
- bsd/kern/sweet_amfi.c: the bsd-phase AMFI/sandbox registration.
- osfmk/arm64/machine_routines.c + iokit/Kernel/IOPlatformExpert.cpp:
  halt_all_cpus and PEHaltRestartInternal - every kPERestartCPU /
  kPEHaltCPU / panic restart passes through the latter - print
  type/details on entry.  This answers "who asked for the reboot".
- osfmk/arm64/sleh.c: one line at the entry of sleh_serror and
  sleh_synchronous (SVC64 excluded so syscalls stay silent) in case
  the death is an exception the kernel sees but never panics from.
- panic freeze (UniXNU-style): with boot-arg sweetpanicfreeze=1,
  panic_trap_to_debugger() calls the new sweet_early_panic_freeze(),
  which forces the early framebuffer console back on, repeats the
  panic reason under a "=== PANIC FREEZE (P0092) ===" banner, masks
  DAIF and sits in wfi - the screen keeps the story and the boot never
  reaches the reboot tail even if something would have wiped it.
  Without the boot-arg nothing changes.

Boot#22 reading table: any terminal "P0092: PEHaltRestartInternal ... /
halt_all_cpus" line names a kernel-driven reset; a terminal P0092 or
SWEET line without a funnel line after it means the kernel died or was
reset from outside xnu; with sweetpanicfreeze=1 any panic shows the
banner instead of silently rebooting.  Other arm64 boards unchanged.

